      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name honors Spanish explorer Don Juan de Oñate, who first mapped the area in the late 1600s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Port_Isabel%2C_Texas",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "During the Civil War, Port Isabel served as a Union supply depot, protecting the Gulf Coast from Confederate raids.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Port_Isabel%2C_Texas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Port Isabel Cultural and Event Center hosts the annual Texas Lighthouse Festival, celebrating the town’s nautical heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://portisabel.com/history/a-guide-to-historical-landmarks-in-port-isabel-walk-through-the-past",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The nearby Treasures of the Gulf Museum showcases artifacts recovered from shipwrecks, linking the town to Gulf maritime history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
